# Panel 244's R1, spec § 13 as it landed on 2026-11-11: "A group's `constant`
# has no body: the header holds the value, in a package named by `version` or
# `git` never a float, a record or one read through an enumerator or object."
# The package here is named by a `path`, so its units build as the program's
# own and its header's float and enumerator are read: it prints 0.5 and 8.
#
# It is the spec-warden's P2 (iii), registered in
# `docs/panel/244-reports/spec-warden.md` § 5 and scored at M-core-packages'
# close: falsified if it flips while the sentence stands. Its twin, P2 (ii),
# is the same two shapes in a fetched package, refused `ffi_constant_type`, in
# `tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2351-a-fetched-constant-only-a-run-could-read-is-refused-never-run.case/`.
use <pk>/pk

function main()
    print(pk.half())
    print(pk.green())
